# ---------------- Arcade_Enemy.events (Task 7 Part G3: arcade lane enemy) ----------------
# No NavMesh, no rays, no waypoints: walk straight at the player on the floor, swing on contact.
# This is the Double Dragon / Contra shape — one polled steering line plus a melee `near`, and
# a spawner (Arcade_Spawner.events) refills the lane.
#
# SETUP (editor): the scene's `Arcade_Enemy` actor is the spawn template — give it an EventSheet
# with Event File = Arcade_Enemy, a BoxCollider, and leave the actor inactive. `spawn Arcade_Enemy
# at SpawnAhead` clones it activated; the clone keeps the template's name (Flax allows duplicate
# actor names), so this one sheet drives every enemy on the floor.
#
# No NavMesh bake is involved: `move toward` is a direct vector, the same word the Variant 1
# chase uses. It walks into walls rather than around them — the documented con of the variant.

when me appears
  enemy type "Zombie"
  print "Arcade_Enemy: walking in"

when every 0.2 seconds
  move toward player speed 100         # re-issued so it tracks a moving player
  # loop anim "Walk"                 # simple meshes have no clips; armature enemies can

when me is near player by 1.5
  my Hostile is true
  # play anim "Attack"
  send message "hurt" to nearest player

# ---- taking a shot ----
# TK_Bullet.events reacts to actors named `Enemy`; the lane names its enemy `Arcade_Enemy`, so
# the hit lands from this side instead: a shot that overlaps costs 10 of the zombie's 50 and is
# used up. Same idea as Enemy.events' damage block, just keyed on the shot rather than a message,
# because a lane full of clones has no single `Enemy` actor to message.
when me touches Bullet
  add -10 to my Health
  destroy other

when my Health becomes 0
  add 1 to kills my Type
  add -1 to EnemiesAlive
  # play anim "Die"
  destroy me
